{"name":"Wood Garlic","hex":"#7a7229","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wood garlic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ramsons."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wood_garlic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Allium ursinum","blocks":[{"text":"Allium ursinum, known as wild garlic, ramsons, cowleekes, cows's leek, cowleek, buckrams, broad-leaved garlic, wood garlic, bear leek, Eurasian wild garlic, onion grass, or bear's garlic, is a bulbous perennial flowering plant in the amaryllis family, Amaryllidaceae. It is native to Eurasia, where it grows in moist woodland. It is a wild relative of onion and garlic, all belonging to the same genus, Allium. There are two recognized subspecies: A. ursinum subsp. ursinum and A. ursinum subsp. ucrainicum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Photo_of_Allium_Ursinum%2C_wild_garlic%2C_north-west_Hampshire%2C_UK%2C_May_2014.jpg/330px-Photo_of_Allium_Ursinum%2C_wild_garlic%2C_north-west_Hampshire%2C_UK%2C_May_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allium_ursinum"},{"title":"Wood","blocks":[{"text":"Wood is a natural, lignocellulosic material derived primarily from the secondary xylem of trees and other woody plants, where it provides mechanical support and in the functional sapwood, conducts water and dissolved minerals. Being a natural material, it is characterized as an organic material – a natural composite of cellulosic fibers that are strong in tension and embedded in a matrix of lignin and hemicelluloses that resists compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/16_wood_samples.jpg/330px-16_wood_samples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood"},{"title":"Garlic","blocks":[{"text":"Garlic is a species of bulbous flowering plants in the genus Allium. Its close relatives include the onion, shallot, leek, chives, Welsh onion, and Chinese onion. Garlic is native to Central Asia, northeastern Iran and the foothills of Himalayas. It has naturalized in many other parts of the world, including Mediterranean Europe and China. There are two subspecies and hundreds of varieties of garlic."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/39/Allium_sativum_Woodwill_1793.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garlic"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/387_Allium_ursinum.jpg/330px-387_Allium_ursinum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/387_Allium_ursinum.jpg/330px-387_Allium_ursinum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A387_Allium_ursinum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Illustration_Allium_ursinum1.jpg/500px-Illustration_Allium_ursinum1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Illustration_Allium_ursinum1.jpg/1280px-Illustration_Allium_ursinum1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Illustration_Allium_ursinum1.jpg/500px-Illustration_Allium_ursinum1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1885 illustration from Otto Wilhelm Thomé","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIllustration_Allium_ursinum1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Allium_ursinum%2C_Arum_maculatum.jpg/500px-Allium_ursinum%2C_Arum_maculatum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimed